---
description: Shadow and spacing conventions for cards, footer bars, and bottom sheets
globs: components/**/*.tsx,app/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# Shadow Conventions

Three named CSS classes cover every surface. Never use inline shadow values for these patterns.

| Surface | Class | When to use |
|---|---|---|
| In-page content card | `card-elevated` | White cards on the `#F1F5FD` / `#F7FAFF` page surface |
| Sticky/fixed footer bar | `footer-elevated` | Fixed bar separating footer from scrollable content |
| Bottom sheet panel | `sheet-elevated` | Modal sheets rising from the bottom |

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<div className="rounded-2xl bg-white card-elevated px-4 py-4">...</div>
<div className="fixed bottom-0 ... footer-elevated">...</div>
<div className="... rounded-t-[24px] bg-white sheet-elevated ...">...</div>

// ❌ BAD — inline shadow values drift over time
<div className="rounded-2xl bg-white shadow-[0_4px_14px_rgba(18,18,18,0.04)] ...">
<div className="fixed bottom-0 shadow-[0_-4px_6px_0_rgba(54,53,76,0.08)] ...">
```

# Concierge Artifact Card Spacing

Values live in `src/styles/_tokens.scss`. Change the token — do not hardcode px in screens.

| Token | Default | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--space-copy-to-card` | 32px | Last body/subtext line → first card |
| `--space-heading-to-card` | 20px | Section heading (headingLastLine) → first card |
| `--space-card-stack` | 24px | Vertical gap between stacked artifact/option cards |
| `--space-car-card-stack` | 20px | Vertical gap between stacked car cards |

```scss
// ✅ GOOD
margin-top: var(--space-copy-to-card);
gap: var(--space-card-stack);
gap: var(--space-car-card-stack);

// ❌ BAD — a one-off px that will drift from the global rule
margin-top: 32px;
gap: calc(var(--spacing) * 6);
```

## Internal rows within a single card

Rows inside a card (e.g., `<dl>`, amount rows) use `gap-3` (12px) or smaller — do not change these. Don't use the stack tokens inside a single card.
